# Reel Deal

## Product

Fisheries and aquaculture relief funded by donations, with public ocean-data
evidence and Solidity settlement. This spec describes repository boundaries;
source presence does not prove a provider is live or a deployment is healthy.
Decision context and consequences live in the [ADRs](../../docs/adrs/README.md),
derived from the inspected code and owning issues. Keep their status separate from
implementation and deployment evidence.

## Observed architecture

- `Contracts`: ReliefPool, HumanRegistry, ENS adapters/interfaces, Foundry tests,
  deployment scripts, and recorded deployments.
- `Shared`: Trigger/EIP-712 types, feed schemas, rules, computation, ABIs, addresses.
- `Pipeline`: existing TypeScript file-backed feed API and pinned buoy, toxin,
  and geographic datasets. Dataset age is not determined by file modification time.
- `Application`: existing Next.js UI, API routes, keeper, identity, and LINE integration.
- `Tooling` and `Documentation`: repository operation and maintained contracts.

## Planned integration

| Planned system | Authoritative tickets | Acceptance boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Astro frontend and app-core | #54, #56, #63 | Preserve existing routes and identity/money behavior |
| FastAPI risk API | #75–#82 | Real heat values with source hashes; shared handoff #55/#79 |
| Postgres app/risk schemas | #57, #59, #62 | Separate app/risk ownership and agreed geographic identity |
| HMI | #32, #36, #40, #47 | Verified datasets first; later station/3D/scenario work |

Plans are not observed source nodes. Update this spec and its source scopes when
implementation lands. GitHub owns task status; do not copy the backlog here.

## Validation

`bun run dog:map` builds the observed inventory. `bun run dog:check` rejects stale
maps, uncovered source files, and source/spec changes since explicit review.
Run domain tests separately: these hashes detect change, not semantic correctness,
ABI compatibility, dataset freshness, or live infrastructure health.
